# Phase 8B Implementation Plan: Real DB Connectors

This phase activates the direct database connection capabilities of the reconciliation tool. We will implement functional adapters for MySQL and PostgreSQL sources, allowing the tool to query live databases instead of relying solely on manual SQL dumps.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Credential Handling**: For this initial implementation, I will assume a "Default Target" strategy using environment variables (`OLD_SOURCE_DB_URL`, `NEW_SOURCE_DB_URL`). This keeps the backend logic clean and secure. We can add a "Connection Modal" to the UI in a subsequent refinement if per-session credentials are required.
>
> **Stability**: The V1 SQL Dump workflow will remain the default and will be untouched.

## Proposed Changes

---

### Backend Components

#### [MODIFY] [requirements.txt](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/Otumisyon/backend/requirements.txt)
- Add `mysql-connector-python` for MySQL support.

#### [NEW] [mysql.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/Otumisyon/backend/app/services/source_adapters/mysql.py)
- Implement `MySQLAdapter`.
- Logic: Connect to a MySQL instance, execute the filtered query, return a normalized DataFrame.
- Driver: `mysql.connector`.

#### [NEW] [postgres.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/Otumisyon/backend/app/services/source_adapters/postgres.py)
- Implement `PostgresAdapter`.
- Logic: Connect to an external PostgreSQL instance (distinct from the internal session restore DB).
- Driver: `psycopg2`.

#### [MODIFY] [factory.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/Otumisyon/backend/app/services/source_adapters/factory.py)
- Update `get_adapter` to instantiate the new real adapters when the source type is `mysql_connection` or `postgres_connection`.

